<title>UK: Libya increases Oct light crudes by 10-15 cents.</title>
<headline>Libya increases Oct light crudes by 10-15 cents.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya's National Oil Corp told contract customers crude prices for October were increased by 10-15 cents a barrel while heavy grades mostly stayed unchanged.</p>
<p>NOC increased Es Sider for October by 15 cents to Dated Brent parity.</p>
<p>Zuetina and Brega both rose 10 cents to Dated Brent plus 40 cents.</p>
<p>Sirtica was increased by 15 cents to Dated Brent plus five cents.  </p>
<p>Heavy grades Amni and Sarir were unchanged at Dated Brent -50 cents and -55 cents respectively.</p>
<p>Bu Attifel was raised five cents to Dated Brent -30 cents.</p>
<p>Offshore crude Bouri was unchanged at Iranian Heavy fob Sidi Kreir -35 cents.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
